      "content": "Definition: Understandability refers to how easily developers can comprehend and maintain the test code.\n\nTask: Improve the understandability of the test `Soundex_ESTest_test09.java` (path:- /Users/tenghaha/Projects/New_Agent_understandability_improvement/data/original/commons-codec/auto/testcases/Soundex_ESTest/Soundex_ESTest_test09.java). The refactored code must be syntactically correct and compilable against the provided CUT signatures. Do not alter the runtime behaviour of the original test: the same methods must be called with the same arguments and produce the same expected outcomes.\n"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It creates a custom `Soundex` with a 9-char mapping, calls `setMaxLength(0)` on the static `US_ENGLISH` instance (accessed confusingly via the local variable), then asserts the local instance's `maxLength` is still 4. I'll rewrite it for clarity.The improved test compiled successfully. The key understandability improvements made were: renaming cryptic variables (`charArray0` → `customMapping`, `soundex0` → `customSoundex`), replacing the confusing instance-access of a static field (`soundex0.US_ENGLISH`) with the proper class-level access (`Soundex.US_ENGLISH`), and adding a comment explaining the intent — that mutating the shared static instance's `maxLength` must not affect an independently constructed `Soundex` instance."
    }
